  "strategy": "# Auto-convolution Minimization Approach\nThis algorithm combines coordinate descent and projected gradient optimization to minimize the self-convolution peak for nonnegative sequences. It uses a warming function to guide the search and prevents getting stuck by clearing the active set periodically.\n\n## Mathematical Specification\nWe seek to minimize: \n    R(a) = 2*n*max(convolve(a,a))/ (sum(a))^2\n\nOver a = [a\u2080,...,a_{n-1}] where:\n- Sum(a) \u2265 0.01 (after clamping to [0,1000])\n- a\u1d62 \u2265 0 for all i\n- convolve(a,a) is the linear convolution (mode='full') producing 2*n-1 coefficients\n\nOur mathematical formulation is:\n    minimize_a R(a)\n    subject_to: sum(a) \u2265 0.01\n                a\u1d62 \u2265 0 for all i\n\nThe optimization is performed by:\n1. Starting from the parent sequence if available\n2. Implementing a coordinate-wise method with temperature parameter T\n3. Using relative-atom descent in active sets based on candidate selection\n4. Periodically clearing active sets to prevent local convergence\n\n## Implementation Procedure\n```python\ndef propose_candidate(seed=42, budget_s=1800):\n    import time\n    import numpy as np\n    \n    # Global access condition for parent sequence\n    if 'height_sequence_1' in globals() and height_sequence_1 is not None:\n        try:\n            px = np.asarray(height_sequence_1, dtype=np.float64)\n            px = np.clip(px, 0.0, 1000.0)\n            n_parent = len(px)\n            # Register sequence length for warm starts\n            px_sum = px.sum()\n            if px_sum < 0.01: \n                # If parent is suboptimal, initialize a better one\n                px = np.ones(n_parent) / n_parent\n                px_sum = px.sum()\n        except Exception:\n            px_sum = None\n    else:\n        px_sum = None\n        n_parent = 100  # Safe default\n    \n    # Initialize best candidate from successful warm start if available\n    best_seq = None\n    best_score = float('inf')\n    deadline = time.time() + 1800  # 30 mins safety margin\n    \n    # Smart initialization based on parent scenario\n    if 'height_sequence_1' in globals() and px_sum is not None:\n        best_seq = np.clip(parent_array, 0, 1000)\n        # If parent was exhausted, don't use it directly\n        # Instead, create many unsuccessful populations for divergence\n        # Set up overlapping samples\n        pass\n    \n    # Strong initialization procedure\n    initial_a = np.ones(n) / n\n    # Modified to feature sharp variations where needed\n\t\n    # Temperature and iteration setup\n    T_val = 0.1  # Initial relative temperature\n    delta_i = 0.05  # Step variation parameter\n    \n    # Main optimization loop\n    while time.time() < deadline:\n        new_a = coordinate_descent(best_seq, T_val)\n        # Evaluate new candidate\n        if optimizes_finite:\n            candidate_score = evaluator(new_a)\n            # Update best if improvement\n            if candidate_score < best_score:\n                best_score = candidate_score\n                best_seq = new_a\n                # Retrain if significantly improved\n        else:\n            # Use defensie fallback to constrainted search\n            new_a = project_to_simplex(new_a, 0.01)\n    \n    return best_seq.tolist()\n    \n    # Detailed function implementations need to be provided below\n    def coordinate_descent(a, T):\n        pass  # Projected gradient implementation\n        \n    def project_to_simplex(a, min_sum):\n        pass  # Euclidean projection with minimum sum constraint\n        \n    def evaluator(a):\n        pass  # Convolve and compute R(a) exactly as in the scoring function\n        \n    def clear_active(a):\n        pass  # Random adjustment to all coordinates to prevent local convergence\n        \n    def check_staleness(a):\n        pass  # History-based stopping condition\n        \n    def global_minimality_check_last_conv_value(a):\n        pass